 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch 24 not draining, water sitting in bottom. help"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can certainly help you with your Bosch dishwasher that isn't draining. The most common cause is simply something blocking the filter or drain pump, though it could also be a kinked hose or a blocked sink waste connection. To sort this out safely, please switch off and unplug the machine first, then twist and lift out the filter at the bottom to clean any food debris from the sump underneath. With the filter removed, look down into the pump area with a torch to see if there is any glass or stone caught in the impeller. Let me know what you find when you check those areas.\n[Helpful to see: image \"Where the filter is\" — The filter sits in the base of the dishwasher, usually under the bottom spray arm. Twist it out anticlockwise and rinse it under a tap. Typical layout — your dishwasher may differ.]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "filter was clogged with food and a bit of broken glass. cleaned it, drains fine now, E:24 gone"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news! It’s very common for food debris or small items like glass to block the filter and cause drainage issues, so clearing it out was exactly the right move. To help prevent this from happening again, I’d recommend scraping your plates thoroughly before loading them into the dishwasher. Is there anything else I can assist you with today?"
  }
 ],
